{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program has no top-level data variables, no sampling statements, no parameters requiring priors, and no prohibited direct log-density manipulation. The transformed-data computation and generated quantity are deterministic and do not condition on protected data.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  // Difference between one-sided Gaussian tail probability and target probability
  vector tail_delta(vector y, vector theta, array[] real x_r, array[] int x_i) {
    vector[1] deltas;
    deltas[1] = 2 * (normal_cdf(theta[1] | 0, exp(y[1])) - 0.5) - 0.99;
    return deltas;
  }
}

transformed data {
  vector[1] y_guess = [log(5)]'; // Initial guess of Gaussian standard deviation
  vector[1] theta = [15]';       // Target quantile
  vector[1] y;
  array[0] real x_r;
  array[0] int x_i;

  // Find Gaussian standard deviation that ensures 99% probabilty below 15
  y = algebra_solver(tail_delta, y_guess, theta, x_r, x_i);

  print("Standard deviation = ", exp(y[1]));
}

generated quantities {
  real sigma = exp(y[1]);
}

","data_safe_json":"{}","protected_variables":[]}
